1. What is a Load Balancer?
A Load Balancer distributes incoming network traffic across multiple servers to ensure high availability, fault tolerance, and better performance.
In Amazon Elastic Load Balancing, the load balancer automatically distributes traffic across multiple EC2 instances.
2. What are the types of Load Balancers in AWS?
AWS provides four types of load balancers in Amazon Elastic Load Balancing:
1️⃣ Application Load Balancer (ALB) – Works at Layer 7 (HTTP/HTTPS)
 2️⃣ Network Load Balancer (NLB) – Works at Layer 4 (TCP/UDP)
 3️⃣ Gateway Load Balancer (GWLB) – Used for security appliances
 4️⃣ Classic Load Balancer (CLB) – Legacy load balancer
